# End-user product rule (Sahi app and anything the driver sees)

Decided 2026-11-21. Full audit and rationale: `Subsystems/Mobile App End-User Scope.md`.

**The audience is the driver of a personal car.** Fleet managers, OEM engineers and the team are
not the audience of the main app. Anything only they need lives in the hidden **Diagnostics** screen
(tap the version number 7 times, labeled "for the Sahi team") or in team tooling, never in the
tabs, onboarding or notifications.

## Audience test (apply to every screen, setting, string and notification)

"Would a driver who has never seen the code know what this is and why they would touch it?" If not:
move it to Diagnostics or delete it.

## Structure

- Three tabs: **Drive**, **Trips**, **Settings**. Driving lock hides everything except the state.
- No "Pi" tab, no health/CPU/throttle/memory/disk, no restart/shutdown, no per-model switches, no
  numeric thresholds, no address entry and no demo mode outside Diagnostics (pairing may offer
  "Having trouble?" for the manual path).
- **Defaults over settings:** good default first, then a 3-way choice (Low / Normal / High), then
  Diagnostics. Never a numeric threshold in the main app.
- **No metric without meaning:** show a state or a plain sentence unless the driver can act on the
  number. Raw EAR / PERCLOS / RR / fps / FOV do not appear in the main app.
- **Live camera video is for setup and calibration only,** not while driving (it distracts).

## Vocabulary (driver-facing copy)

| Never | Say |
|---|---|
| Pi, Raspberry Pi, fusion, model, MJPEG, fps, EAR, PERCLOS, RR, throttled | your Sahi unit, camera, alert, eyes closed, heart rate |
| monitoring paused (technical) | "Sahi stopped monitoring at 14:32 because your phone closed it. Tap to fix." |
| offline / not paired | "Unit not connected. Check it is powered on." |
| error codes, HTTP/BLE terms | what happened and the one thing to do |

English only, plain words, specific, short. Alerts say why in one line.

## Review gate

Every UI PR body must include: "Audience check: <screens touched> pass the audience test; engineer
items moved to Diagnostics: <list or none>". Reviewers reject a PR that adds an admin/engineer item
to a main screen.
